    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d686">

                <pb facs="0580" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11988.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Fletcher to the Secretary of the Navy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Florida, <lb/> Vera
                            Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1914-04-15T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On April 14, in answer to specific questions, have obtained from Mayo following
                    answers: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Our boats daily used regular landing during attack [of
                            Constitutionalists] on Tampico, without objection previous to the
                            arrest. No notice that other landings were forbidden had been given. We
                            were never requested to give notice nor obtain permission before landing
                            boats’ crews. I received no notice that hostilities existed. The only
                            restriction imposed upon our movements was a refusal to pass through the
                            [Federal] lines to deliver letter to Rebels. I will also transmit the
                            foregoing to the American Embassy. Foreign warships report same
                            conditions.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
